From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: turbinebmw <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Crop by default, raw TNR and chroma
 NR

Three changes to the CPU debayer:

- Field of view. Binning the whole sensor for small outputs gives the
  widest view, which is too wide for a front camera on video calls.
  Crop the centre at full resolution by default, and bin only when
  LIBCAMERA_SOFTISP_FOV=wide or `fov=wide` in
  $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sp12/camera.conf, read at each configure so a change
  applies the next time a camera starts.

- Temporal noise reduction on the unbinned path. Filter unpacked raw
  lines as they are copied for debayering, with the binned path's
  thresholds (each binned colour is also a single raw sample), after lens
  shading. Each thread filters only the rows it outputs, so each history
  row has one writer. Frame-to-frame noise on the cropped front camera
  drops by about 40% at 30 fps; the rear camera, which is never soft
  binned, gets TNR too.

- Chroma noise reduction on the output. The chroma (B - Y, R - Y) of each
  2x2 block goes through a 5x5 sigma filter at half resolution, averaging
  only neighbours within a threshold (default 8, LIBCAMERA_SOFTISP_CNR, 0
  turns it off), and is recombined with each pixel's own luma after
  bilinear upsampling. It runs in three passes over all threads after
  debayering, about 2 ms per 1080p frame with four threads. Colour
  speckle on flat areas drops by about 40%; a threshold of 20 halved it
  but flattened skin tones and lost a blind comparison, 8 won one.
